{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478766-when-is-an-effect-counted-for-the-multiple-effects-modifier","id":1478766,"title":"When is an Effect counted for the multiple Effects modifier?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-13T08:10:47-07:00","id":1478766,"title":"When is an Effect counted for the multiple Effects modifier?","content":"So, M20 Page 528 through 529 talks about Effects and that for every 2 effects running adds +1 to difficulty. It then goes on to explain this only applies to Effects that require &quot;ongoing concentration&quot; and gives a couple of examples &quot;summoning, a force field, weather control.&quot; It further explains that Effects that have &quot;Time-based trigger, one which is locked into another pattern, or one that has been cast but whose duration has not expired, does not count.<br /> <br /> So...every Effect (rote) I have seen seems to fit into each of those exceptions. Is there a &quot;concentration&quot; time modifier that I am missing, because they all seem to be instant unless successes are spent to raise duration.<br /> <br /> I am confused...if I am missing something, I am sorry.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T19:48:38-07:00","id":1478815,"title":"","content":"You haven't missed anything. Normally effects in mage are fire and forget unless a mage's paradigm calls for otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what exactly the designers were going for with that specific rule, but it basically doesn't apply to 90% of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T20:16:05-07:00","id":1478816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leofwyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478766-when-is-an-effect-counted-for-the-multiple-effects-modifier#post1478766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, M20 Page 528 through 529 talks about Effects and that for every 2 effects running adds +1 to difficulty. It then goes on to explain this only applies to Effects that require &quot;ongoing concentration&quot; and gives a couple of examples &quot;summoning, a force field, weather control.&quot; It further explains that Effects that have &quot;Time-based trigger, one which is locked into another pattern, or one that has been cast but whose duration has not expired, does not count.<br /> <br /> So...every Effect (rote) I have seen seems to fit into each of those exceptions. Is there a &quot;concentration&quot; time modifier that I am missing, because they all seem to be instant unless successes are spent to raise duration.<br /> <br /> I am confused...if I am missing something, I am sorry.<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, any effect that requires the mage concentration. For example telekinesis: controling an object/being for some time. Or illusions that you don't want to stay static or doing something pre defined, this way you can change it according to what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T17:01:43-07:00","id":1478924,"title":"","content":"Thank you!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T23:32:58-07:00","id":1479001,"title":"","content":"The 'Locking Magickal Effects' paragraph also elaborates on this.<br /> <br /> With Forces 2 you can technically put an invisibility field around a person - but since that effect is not locked onto anything, if that person moves, they just walk out of the invisibility field. The Mage has to actively concentrate to keep the field up and move it with that person. Effects like this count against the multiple effects rule.<br /> <br /> However, if you use Forces 2 and Life (or Matter for objects, Correspondence for locations..), you can lock that effect onto the person - the field will become Fire And Forget. It will stay up and will move with that person, without requiring the Mage to concentrate on the effect - this effect does *not* count against the multiple effects rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/